cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its method or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "trust-me-bro: a paired benchmark of token-saving tools for coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: malochapo
repository-code: "https://github.com/malochapo/trust-me-bro"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
abstract: >-
  Runs Claude Code on the same tasks and code base with and without tools that
  claim to cut what coding agents cost (rtk, Headroom, lean-ctx, sobre), and
  compares billed tokens and task success. Follow-up tests measure what loading
  MCP tools up front and where a long session is compacted change in a run's
  cost. Every run is published with its transcript.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - coding agents
  - Claude Code
  - LLM cost
  - token usage
  - prompt caching
